.TH FILEGEN 1 "January 2026" "filegen" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
filegen \- generate files from templates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B filegen
.I NAME
.I DEST
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B filegen
.BR shell
.br
.B filegen
.BR help
.SH DESCRIPTION
filegen generates files from templates located in a repo-specific templates
directory. If no file-type flags are provided, all discovered types are
generated. It was built with C source/header generation in mind, but can be
extended to any file type by adding templates.
.SH INSTALLATION
Install uv:
.nf
.RS
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh
.RE
.fi
One way to install (not the only way):
.nf
.RS
chmod +x filegen
mv filegen ~/.local/bin/filegen
.RE
.fi
Install the man page:
.nf
.RS
install -m 644 filegen.1 ~/\.local/share/man/man1/
.RE
.fi
If your MANPATH does not include ~/.local/share/man, add it:
.nf
.RS
export MANPATH="${MANPATH}:$HOME/.local/share/man"
.RE
.fi
.SH CONFIGURATION
Template directory resolution order:
.IP 1.
--template-dir
.IP 2.
FILEGEN_TEMPLATES
.IP 3.
<repo-root>/templates (repo-root detected by a .git directory)
.PP
You can set the environment variable:
.nf
.RS
export FILEGEN_TEMPLATES=/path/to/templates
.RE
.fi
.SH TEMPLATE DISCOVERY
Templates are resolved in this order:
.IP 1.
--template-dir
.IP 2.
FILEGEN_TEMPLATES
.IP 3.
<repo-root>/templates (repo-root detected by a .git directory)
.PP
Templates must include YAML-style frontmatter with a filetype field:
.nf
.RS
---
filetype: c
---
.RE
.fi
Template file extensions must match the type:
.IP \[bu] 2
*.ctf for C source (filetype: c)
.IP \[bu] 2
*.htf for C header (filetype: h)
.PP
Required template variables:
.IP \[bu] 2
Header (.htf): ${file_name}, ${header_guard}, ${year}
.IP \[bu] 2
Source (.ctf): ${file_name}, ${year}
.PP
Other file types are discoverable but generation is currently limited to c/h.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -t , " " --type " " TYPE
Generate files matching TYPE (repeatable, supports TYPE=all).
.TP
.BR --type-add " " PATH
Add a template file for this run (repeatable).
.TP
.BR -t , " " --template-dir " " DIR
Use DIR for templates (overrides FILEGEN_TEMPLATES and repo templates).
.TP
.BR -r , " " --root " " DIR
Root directory for header guards (defaults to DEST parent).
.TP
.BR -f , " " --force
Overwrite existing files without prompting.
.SH INTERACTIVE SHELL
.B filegen shell
starts an interactive session where you can run multiple generate commands
without reloading the script.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate all discovered types (default):
.nf
.RS
filegen my_module ./src
.RE
.fi
Generate only a header:
.nf
.RS
filegen my_module ./include -t h
.RE
.fi
Generate only a source file:
.nf
.RS
filegen my_module ./src -t c
.RE
.fi
Use repo templates:
.nf
.RS
filegen my_module ./src
.RE
.fi
Use explicit template directory:
.nf
.RS
filegen my_module ./src --template-dir ./templates
.RE
.fi
Interactive shell for batch creation:
.nf
.RS
filegen shell
# then run: generate my_module ./src -t c -t h
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uv (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Internal tool.
